15 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a multi-step process for managing wheat diseases. Steps include Text Chunking \(highlighting pesticide use for smut prevention\), Entity Extraction \(identifies wheat, diseases, pests, control methods\), Element Summarization \(focus on wheat powdery mildew\), Graph Communities \(visual links between elements like pest and fungus\), and Query Answering \(using a language model to find solutions for reducing wheat diseases\). Includes pruning algorithm and aphid control context.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating data processing. Unstructured data is converted to CSV format, leading to Chunk 1, which involves pruning fruit trees and removing cocoons. Next is Chunk 2, created by overlapping data, and including summer agricultural practices. Data is then grouped by ID.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Two network diagrams composed of numerous multicolored circles connected by lines, representing complex interconnected systems. The left diagram appears slightly less dense than the right.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Two donut charts display distributions. The left chart represents entity types: Crops in pink, Diseases in purple, Pests in yellow, Control Measures in green, and Others in blue. The right chart shows relation types: Disease Infects Crop in yellow, Pest Harms Crop in green, Control Targets Pest/Disease in blue, Disease-Environment in maroon, and Other Relations in teal.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Instructions for hawthorn pest control are presented in two sections. The left section details chemical control methods, listing recommended pesticides like Niprofren, Avermectin, and Permethrin, along with their specific dosages. The right section discusses biological and chemical control methods for disease and pest prevention in hawthorns, emphasizing eco-friendly practices and comprehensive approaches to minimize environmental impact while protecting yield. Visual icons of pests and a pesticide bottle accompany the text.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Bar charts displaying performance metrics for four models: RAG, GraphRAG-wo-Community, GraphRAG-wo-Knowledge Graph, and Crop GraphRAG. Metrics include Accuracy, Recall, F1, BLEU Score, and Average Response Time. Crop GraphRAG consistently shows the highest scores in accuracy, recall, F1, and BLEU, while having the longest response time. Error bars are present for precision measurement.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing four models \(DeepSeek-R1, BM25+LLM, Naive RAG, Crop GraphRAG\) across four evaluation metrics: Accuracy, Coverage, Relevance, and Traceability. Crop GraphRAG consistently scores highest. Models are color-coded: orange \(DeepSeek-R1\), gray \(BM25+LLM\), light gray \(Naive RAG\), blue \(Crop GraphRAG\). Error bars indicate variability. Statistical significance is denoted by letters and asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
